   "message": "docs(issue17): bind slice-28 mutation evidence to the reviewed engine bytes\n\nThe retained mutation RED logs were captured before cargo fmt reformatted\nengine.rs, so they recorded a sha256 that no longer matched the reviewed tree\n(found by the independent review of 38dc519, non-blocking). Regenerated at\n38dc519: every log now records engine.rs sha256 7439a45c\u2026 before and after the\nmutation, and run-mutations.py still proves the byte-for-byte restore.\n\nAlso discloses the one ordering limit the reviewer named: the printed layer 7b\nsetter is applied before one-shot setters regardless of timestamp, which no card\nin this pool can observe but a future mass base-P/T setter would.",
